From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp90: Implement the concurrent_queue iterator base and the NFS allocator.

concurrent_queue's iterator base and the containers' cache line allocator
were spec stubs in msvcp100 .. msvcp120 and concrt140 (msvcp120_app
forwards). _Concurrent_queue_iterator_base_v4 (constructor, destructor,
_Assign, _Advance) walks the positions between the queue's head and tail,
finding each item where _Internal_push put it (sub-queue position % 8,
page slot position / 8), and points at nothing at the end. NFS_Allocate
returns blocks that start on a 128-byte line (NFS_GetLineSize), with
bad_alloc on an overflowing size, and NFS_Free frees them. The two copies
of details.c (msvcp90, concrt140) change alike.
